  "prompts": {
    "EXPLAIN_INSTRUCTION": "Explain in 2-4 sentences, for a test engineer, what this test checks, why it matters for the requirement, and what outcome is expected. Do not invent byte values.",
    "PARSE_INSTRUCTION": "Extract the UDS identifiers in requirement_text, using only keys from spec_index. Work in this order and add nothing the text does not mention or clearly imply.\n1. services: the service for the main action (never empty). read/report a value -> 0x22; write/set/change a value or calibration -> 0x2E; switch/enter/return to a session or mode -> 0x10; unlock/seed/key -> 0x27; ECU reset/reboot -> 0x11; keep-alive/tester present -> 0x3E; start/stop/results of a routine or self-test -> 0x31; read fault memory/trouble codes -> 0x19; clear them -> 0x14.\n2. dids / routines: match the words of the text to the names in spec_index (a stored setting is a DID, something started or run is a routine). Only values the text names.\n3. sessions: default -> 0x01, programming/flash -> 0x02, extended/diagnostic mode -> 0x03. Also add service 0x10 only if being in that session is a condition ('shall require extended mode', 'only in the flash session'); 'in any/every session' is not.\n4. security: only if the text mentions unlock, security access, seed/key or a level: add service 0x27 and the level (level 1 -> 0x01, programming-level -> 0x03). Otherwise leave security_levels empty and do not add 0x27.\n5. intents from allowed_intents, 2-4 keywords.\nExamples (other requirements; never copy their identifiers):\n'Vehicle speed shall be readable in every session.' -> services [0x22], dids [0x0140], sessions [0x01,0x02,0x03]\n'The door actuator calibration must give results only after it was started.' -> services [0x31], routines [0x0202]\n'Changing the ambient colour shall need extended mode and a level 1 unlock.' -> services [0x10,0x27,0x2E], dids [0x0101], sessions [0x03], security_levels [0x01]",
    "PLAN_COMPACT_TEMPLATE": "OPTIONS (the only choices allowed; answer with a template_id and one of its option_index values):\n{options}\n\n{history}REQUIREMENT {requirement_id}: {requirement_text}\nPARSED: {parsed}\n\nTASK: {instruction}",
    "PLAN_INSTRUCTION": "Choose test cases that verify the requirement thoroughly: positive behaviour plus negative, session, security and timing checks where relevant. Each choice is a template_id from the catalog and an option_index from that template's options, with a one-sentence rationale. Do not repeat choices listed under rejected or already_kept.",
    "SCHEMA_RETRY_INSTRUCTION": "Your previous reply was not valid JSON for the required schema. Error: {error}\nReply again with only a JSON object that matches the schema.",
    "SYSTEM_PROMPT": "You are a UDS (ISO 14229) diagnostics test-planning assistant for an automotive ECU. You never write request or response bytes. You only reference identifiers that exist in the provided spec index, choose template ids and option indices from the provided catalog, and write short plain-English prose. Answer with JSON matching the schema when one is required."
  },
